			<div class="content" id="post-content-4854325">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Emotional</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> The &quot;standard&quot; SCP article format, with a description and then test logs hidden in a collapsible. The test logs will be formatted:</p>
<div class="code">
<pre>
<code>Subject:
Items:
[Location]:Item
...
Afterwards:</code>
</pre></div>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A road on which objects relating to your past dreams, goals, and desires appear (out of reach). As you walk along it, past burdens are &quot;freed&quot; from you.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Disconnected stories of the people that walk on the road, told by the objects that they encounter. For instance:</p>
<ul>
<li>An burnt out ethics committee member who wanted to &quot;bring justice&quot; when he was younger (a discolored robe, a trap with a hole in it, a corroded pen,&#8230;, a colorless foundation site), after stepping off of the road he resigns from the foundation.</li>
<li>A terrorist who was a revolutionary. (A torn police cap, burnt money, a rusted guillotine,&#8230;, his own corpse), who puts up less resistance after.</li>
<li>A doctor who wanted to save lives. (A firefighter coat, a broken down gravestone,&#8230;, a hospital in the distance). Returned to foundation work with increased score on the Foundation Personnel Wellness Exam.</li>
<li>&#8230;</li>
</ul>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> This SCP aims to tell the story of people's lives through the test logs, which are just lists of items, without the &quot;human&quot; in them. There are no notes on theorized meanings, and the reader is free to draw their own conclusion from the objects and their location on the road.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I don't quite know how &quot;strong(?)&quot; to make the effect of giving up your past dreams yet. I also don't know if I want to go for the more metaphorical meaning with the items (a clipped bird symbolizing lack of freedom, etc.) or with objects that they used to try to achieve their dreams (the gavel of a judge, etc.).</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
<em>As a courtesy to our readers on mobile devices, please collapse long posts. ~Zyn</em>
